WEBVTT

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:05.400
The AV-98,
aka the Ingram patrol labor.

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:08.520
6.02 tons.
8.02 meters high.

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:12.700
SCB powered.
SCLM drive system.

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:15.990
Armed and ready for combat with a
37 millimeter revolver and stun baton.

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:19.540
Designed specifically
for police use...

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:22.200
to make a psychological impact
on the community...

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:25.540
to deter criminals
while making the public feel safe.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:51.280
yume wo sutenaide
You must not let go of your dreams

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:54.070
me wo sorasanaide
And never turn your gaze away

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:59.080
futari no ai mo kumoru yo
Yet even still love may cloud up and fade away

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:03.450
utsumuita kata wo
And even though you comforted your love

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:06.290
dakishimeta keredo
When he was feeling down

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:11.300
samishisa mune ni tsumotta
Sadness was still weighing down his heavy heart

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:18.510
yume wa kimi no buki no hazu da yo
Hang on tight to your dreams - they're weapons in your arsenal

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:25.270
nee da kara kanashimi mo kinukete itte
You'll find that you can get through anything at all

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:31.440
so never cry itsu mo kimi wo mitsumete 'ru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be watching over you

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:37.280
fair na ikikata no kimi ga suki
What I love about you is your strong sense of fairness

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:43.790
so never cry itsu mo kimi no soba ni iru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be right there by your side

00:01:44.410 --> 00:01:49.460
da kara mata asu e kakedashite
And so now you can face your future fearlessly

00:01:57.010 --> 00:02:01.010
Target: Captain Goto

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:32.170
Cute letter.
From your niece?

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:34.920
Not sure.

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:49.770
"Die."

00:02:50.310 --> 00:02:52.690
She's asking
for a favor, I suppose?

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:56.230
That's one way
of looking at it, I guess.

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:58.570
Hey, you're late!

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:01.740
We work hard here.
How do you expect us to keep going?

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:05.200
Sorry. We had a rush
just as I was leaving.

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:10.040
Three fried rice, three ramen,
one tempura, and two specials.

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:10.960
That's everything.

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:13.670
Thanks again!

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:19.090
Hey, is my tempura here too?

00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:20.590
Over there.

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:27.890
Did they forget the MSG?

00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:30.020
That bad?

00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:32.020
Mine tastes like always.

00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:37.520
Serves you right.

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:41.280
You shouldn't wolf your food down.
No one's gonna steal it!

00:03:51.910 --> 00:03:54.710
Might as well pay homage
to the Section Chief.

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:56.000
Oh, is he here?

00:03:56.590 --> 00:03:57.670
Yeah, for once.

00:03:58.500 --> 00:04:00.920
At least wear your shoes.

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:02.760
You can't scuff in
with those slippers.

00:04:05.090 --> 00:04:06.430
Right, good idea.

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:11.640
I hear that Division 2 is
due for another evaluation.

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:12.810
Captain Goto, you must've heard.

00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:14.140
Really? It is?

00:04:14.140 --> 00:04:15.520
Yes.

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:19.480
And I don't think your
conduct is going to help, either.

00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:21.610
That topic will certainly come up.

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:24.240
What's wrong?

00:04:25.660 --> 00:04:27.120
Cat droppings.

00:04:28.490 --> 00:04:31.660
I hate to sound like
a junior high school principal...

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:35.620
but keeping a trim uniform is
the first step to doing a good job.

00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:45.590
Yeah, right.

00:04:46.090 --> 00:04:48.760
I have no shortage of enemies,
that's for certain.

00:05:00.270 --> 00:05:01.360
Oops, sorry!

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:04.610
My fault. I was just
throwing away my cigarette.

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:06.860
But I'd better not litter.

00:05:09.530 --> 00:05:10.830
The meeting's about to start.

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:14.370
Oh, sorry!
Forgot all about it.

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:23.130
You must be imagining things.

00:05:23.380 --> 00:05:26.260
I believe I know something
of the martial arts...

00:05:26.260 --> 00:05:28.720
and he's suddenly
carrying himself oddly.

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:32.390
Well, could it be
that you just misunderstood.

00:05:32.390 --> 00:05:37.230
How much do you really
know about Captain Goto?

00:05:37.230 --> 00:05:38.940
Don't you think
he's been acting strange lately?

00:05:38.940 --> 00:05:41.150
He doesn't seem himself
as far as I'm concerned.

00:05:43.650 --> 00:05:45.070
Now that you mention it...

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:48.280
He hasn't been taking
his regular naps.

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:51.740
And he didn't finish his tempura
the other day.

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:55.370
There must be something
wrong with him.

00:05:56.370 --> 00:05:59.460
"Kiichi Goto and the Case of
the Disappearing Appetite."

00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:02.750
What secrets lurk in
his mysterious past?

00:06:02.750 --> 00:06:07.420
Sounds interesting;
just like a Nancy Drew mystery.

00:06:11.510 --> 00:06:12.430
Let's get on it!

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:17.140
Twenty laps around the building?

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:18.140
Me?

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:22.820
We want to hold a training
marathon for the entire team...

00:06:22.860 --> 00:06:25.030
to improve our health,
and we'd like you to participate!

00:06:25.070 --> 00:06:26.650
Okay, I'll be the finish-line judge.

00:06:26.650 --> 00:06:27.860
But then we won't know...
Oops...!

00:06:27.860 --> 00:06:28.900
- Huh?
- I mean...

00:06:28.900 --> 00:06:32.660
This will build unity.
We want you to be part of it!

00:06:33.910 --> 00:06:35.330
I guess it wouldn't hurt.

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:41.750
I don't get it. What are we
killing ourselves for?

00:06:42.130 --> 00:06:44.960
Are you sure this has to do
with his health? What'dya think?

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:45.840
Pipe down Asuma!

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:49.720
This is the best way to evaluate
the captain's health and fitness.

00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:54.260
All set?

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:55.970
On your mark!

00:06:56.270 --> 00:06:58.680
Ready!
Go!

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:04.270
He's fast!

00:07:06.110 --> 00:07:07.320
Pace yourself;
we've got a long way to go.

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:23.250
What? Are you done already?

00:07:23.830 --> 00:07:26.880
Hanging around young
people is bad for your health.

00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:35.350
This is what we get for forgetting to take
his quirky personality into account.

00:07:36.430 --> 00:07:40.270
So why did WE run
the 20 laps for real?

00:07:40.730 --> 00:07:41.980
Because we're idiots!

00:07:43.810 --> 00:07:44.730
That's right!

00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:46.320
This time he can't hide!

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:47.020
How?

00:07:49.570 --> 00:07:51.990
Kendo? But I'm self-taught.

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:53.490
That's all right.

00:07:53.490 --> 00:07:55.620
During my stay in Japan...

00:07:55.620 --> 00:07:58.580
I would really like to learn
the traditional martial arts.

00:08:00.330 --> 00:08:01.290
Well, I suppose.

00:08:01.290 --> 00:08:02.660
Thank you very much.

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:08.340
What's up?

00:08:08.340 --> 00:08:10.300
Are they suddenly
showing some initiative?

00:08:11.170 --> 00:08:13.630
Maybe they're more likable
than they seem.

00:08:33.450 --> 00:08:35.950
Full point.
Excellent strike.

00:08:40.990 --> 00:08:43.460
No, I can't do it;
I wouldn't dream of it.

00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:46.960
You're the only one who can, Hiromi!

00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:47.960
Yeah!

00:08:50.880 --> 00:08:53.590
Well, I can't tell you much.

00:08:54.380 --> 00:08:57.550
He was well known before I got here.

00:08:57.760 --> 00:09:00.560
His reputation was pretty bad.

00:09:01.100 --> 00:09:02.060
Right.

00:09:02.810 --> 00:09:06.520
Why are you suddenly so
curious about his background?

00:09:06.770 --> 00:09:10.940
Oh, no reason in particular.

00:09:10.940 --> 00:09:12.440
It's just that...

00:09:12.860 --> 00:09:16.700
Well, what do you know! Speak
of the devil, and who should appear!

00:09:16.950 --> 00:09:18.530
Why don't you ask him yourself?

00:09:18.870 --> 00:09:21.160
What is this?

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:23.450
What happened here?

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:26.460
A potted plant fell from the sky.

00:09:26.750 --> 00:09:27.920
That was quite the shock.

00:09:27.920 --> 00:09:31.040
This is no joke, this is serious!

00:09:31.340 --> 00:09:32.380
Where did it happen?

00:09:32.380 --> 00:09:35.130
This isn't some cheap, thriller flick!

00:09:35.380 --> 00:09:37.930
Okay, it hit me on the highway.

00:09:39.140 --> 00:09:40.760
No sense looking for the perp, though.

00:09:40.760 --> 00:09:43.020
The truck's long gone.

00:09:43.020 --> 00:09:45.270
This patrol car's an eyesore, now.

00:09:45.270 --> 00:09:46.390
Spiff it up, would ya?

00:09:50.360 --> 00:09:52.650
Captain, where's the perp?

00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:54.570
Be right with you.

00:09:56.570 --> 00:10:00.120
The attack on his patrol car
seems too coincidental.

00:10:00.120 --> 00:10:02.740
What's the deal with that guy?

00:10:02.740 --> 00:10:04.660
He said it was an accident.

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:08.920
False alarm, I suppose.

00:10:09.170 --> 00:10:09.670
Let's go.

00:10:09.830 --> 00:10:10.710
Roger!

00:10:14.550 --> 00:10:15.380
Strange...

00:10:17.380 --> 00:10:18.090
Hang on!

00:10:18.590 --> 00:10:21.430
How embarrassing calling
us out on a false alarm!

00:10:21.430 --> 00:10:23.720
At least it was nothing serious.

00:10:23.720 --> 00:10:27.100
Nothing serious?
But they got us all fired up for nothing!

00:10:30.520 --> 00:10:31.610
Ota...

00:10:33.570 --> 00:10:36.900
Sorry, I'm having problems
with the hydraulics.

00:10:40.410 --> 00:10:41.240
What's wrong?

00:10:41.240 --> 00:10:42.570
How did this happen?

00:10:55.710 --> 00:11:00.180
That's no practical joke.
Nobody noticed a thing?

00:11:00.180 --> 00:11:03.680
Sorry, but I'm gonna have to
ask you some questions.

00:11:04.140 --> 00:11:05.140
Fire away.

00:11:05.720 --> 00:11:08.480
Well, Mr. Sakaki,
have you noticed anything odd...

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:10.730
happening around Captain Goto?

00:11:11.100 --> 00:11:13.690
I can't say that I have.

00:11:13.690 --> 00:11:17.360
Oh, I was hoping you might
know something, Mr. Sakaki.

00:11:17.650 --> 00:11:22.530
You should ask
Captain Goto himself.

00:11:22.910 --> 00:11:24.030
Well, go on.

00:11:24.030 --> 00:11:26.200
I have work to do.

00:11:28.080 --> 00:11:30.750
This is all connected, somehow.

00:11:30.790 --> 00:11:34.170
That's the only explanation
for all the accidents around here:

00:11:34.750 --> 00:11:38.460
The flower pot on the patrol car,
the false alarm, the leaking hydraulics.

00:11:38.460 --> 00:11:43.010
They were all deliberate
acts of malice.

00:11:43.720 --> 00:11:49.140
And they all started after
Captain Goto began acting strangely.

00:11:49.520 --> 00:11:52.980
But we still don't have a clue
about what's going on!

00:11:52.980 --> 00:11:54.650
That's true.

00:12:00.990 --> 00:12:06.830
Captain Goto, your team has been
interested in some odd things lately.

00:12:06.830 --> 00:12:08.540
They're just playing detective.

00:12:09.330 --> 00:12:11.960
I don't want to sound
like a nagging mother...

00:12:11.960 --> 00:12:15.670
but shouldn't you get ready
for your efficiency report?

00:12:16.170 --> 00:12:19.250
I saw your report, and noticed
that your ratings have fallen.

00:12:19.500 --> 00:12:21.880
Too late to do anything about that.

00:12:21.880 --> 00:12:24.130
It's like locking the barn
after the horse is gone.

00:12:24.720 --> 00:12:27.970
If my team's efficiency is down,
they're not the ones to blame.

00:12:29.180 --> 00:12:30.640
You're so laid back.

00:12:43.650 --> 00:12:46.530
Labor X

00:12:47.910 --> 00:12:51.290
Subject located.
About to commence pursuit.

00:12:51.790 --> 00:12:53.960
Roger. Good luck.

00:12:56.420 --> 00:12:57.420
Is he still there?

00:12:57.420 --> 00:12:59.710
Yeah. He's coming out.

00:13:02.340 --> 00:13:06.130
"Bookstore: Purchased
one periodical."

00:13:06.470 --> 00:13:07.510
Get down!

00:13:08.350 --> 00:13:09.760
That hurt, you know!

00:13:09.760 --> 00:13:11.470
Can't you walk without talking?

00:13:11.470 --> 00:13:12.520
Lighten up!

00:13:16.730 --> 00:13:17.690
You idiot!

00:13:17.690 --> 00:13:18.940
Trying to get yourself killed?

00:13:27.570 --> 00:13:29.910
Excuse me! Sorry!

00:13:30.200 --> 00:13:31.580
Quiet down!

00:13:31.910 --> 00:13:35.330
We're tailing someone!
We have to be inconspicuous.

00:13:37.670 --> 00:13:39.840
What are you doing?

00:13:39.840 --> 00:13:41.130
I'm sorry!

00:13:44.920 --> 00:13:46.220
Hey, pick these up!

00:13:46.220 --> 00:13:49.340
Maybe he'll do us a favor and head home.

00:13:49.890 --> 00:13:51.050
Only kidding...

00:13:51.760 --> 00:13:53.180
Oh, he stopped!

00:13:53.680 --> 00:13:54.520
All right.

00:13:56.100 --> 00:13:59.190
"Subject conversed with
female rice-cake dealer."

00:13:59.560 --> 00:14:04.610
"Approximate age: 76.
Conversation topic: Unknown."

00:14:05.110 --> 00:14:07.570
You mean you can't
read his mind, Kanuka?

00:14:08.780 --> 00:14:09.780
Spare me.

00:14:13.030 --> 00:14:15.660
Well, he sure looks
pretty ordinary to me.

00:14:15.910 --> 00:14:17.540
I'm with you on that one.

00:14:20.420 --> 00:14:21.210
Hi.

00:14:21.920 --> 00:14:23.670
Oh, Captain Goto!

00:14:23.670 --> 00:14:24.210
How are you?

00:14:24.960 --> 00:14:26.760
You must be tired
after all that walking.

00:14:26.970 --> 00:14:28.170
How about grabbing a bite.

00:14:34.720 --> 00:14:35.970
What's wrong?
Not going to eat?

00:14:36.600 --> 00:14:38.140
Sure, I am.

00:14:38.140 --> 00:14:40.940
It's just that I'm afraid we must
look like complete idiots.

00:14:41.350 --> 00:14:42.360
Relax.

00:14:42.610 --> 00:14:45.150
The other guy tailing me is
even more obvious than you two.

00:14:46.400 --> 00:14:47.320
Really?!

00:14:47.690 --> 00:14:50.530
Don't look right at him, stupid!

00:14:55.410 --> 00:14:56.490
Come on in!

00:14:57.290 --> 00:14:58.580
Who is he?

00:14:59.120 --> 00:15:00.790
You don't recognize him?

00:15:01.290 --> 00:15:03.460
Now that you mention it...
No.

00:15:05.050 --> 00:15:08.260
Has he also... I mean... Has he been
following you all this time?

00:15:08.260 --> 00:15:08.720
Yeah.

00:15:08.720 --> 00:15:09.420
He's suspicious!

00:15:09.880 --> 00:15:10.880
Hang tight.

00:15:10.880 --> 00:15:13.050
He hasn't played his trump card yet.

00:15:18.640 --> 00:15:22.150
"Paid for meal, took receipt,
and returned home."

00:15:22.810 --> 00:15:24.810
This doesn't answer anything!

00:15:24.810 --> 00:15:27.690
Incompetent nitwits!
What were you doing?!

00:15:27.690 --> 00:15:29.400
Let's see you do better!

00:15:29.400 --> 00:15:31.200
Don't give me that attitude!

00:15:31.200 --> 00:15:34.780
In any case, he's onto us.

00:15:34.780 --> 00:15:38.240
Now that the Captain
knows, our plan is ruined.

00:15:39.290 --> 00:15:40.870
There's another way!

00:15:40.870 --> 00:15:41.500
Huh?

00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:43.330
The way I see it...

00:15:43.330 --> 00:15:47.750
your mystery man is clearly
linked to all the pranks.

00:15:47.750 --> 00:15:49.920
All we have to do
is snag him. It's easy.

00:15:49.920 --> 00:15:51.680
And do what with him?

00:15:51.680 --> 00:15:54.930
The captain ordered us
to leave him alone.

00:15:54.930 --> 00:15:57.260
Besides, there's no way to find him.

00:15:57.720 --> 00:15:59.930
We'll just bend the rules a bit!

00:15:59.930 --> 00:16:03.480
The instant you see him, grab
him and force him to confess!

00:16:03.480 --> 00:16:05.110
That's the only way!

00:16:05.110 --> 00:16:07.730
You've got all the bright ideas;
you do it!

00:16:07.730 --> 00:16:09.190
Who, me?!

00:16:09.190 --> 00:16:12.570
Instead of arguing, how about
spending your time cleaning up in here?

00:16:13.200 --> 00:16:14.570
Cleaning up?

00:16:14.860 --> 00:16:16.070
Again?

00:16:16.070 --> 00:16:20.330
The chief is coming in for
an inspection tomorrow.

00:16:20.330 --> 00:16:22.500
Lucky for us, he'll probably
give us a lecture.

00:16:22.960 --> 00:16:23.790
Ugh.

00:16:23.960 --> 00:16:27.040
The least we can do is
tidy up the room for him.

00:16:27.040 --> 00:16:28.000
Now, get to it.

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:29.340
Yes, sir.

00:16:31.090 --> 00:16:32.510
Saved! Time to mobilize!

00:16:34.010 --> 00:16:36.220
Excuse me, please.
Let me through.

00:16:37.550 --> 00:16:39.180
What exactly happened here?

00:16:39.180 --> 00:16:42.890
A girder fell on a parked car.

00:16:43.520 --> 00:16:45.940
They started arguing
about whose fault it was...

00:16:46.150 --> 00:16:47.560
and their tempers flared up.

00:16:48.190 --> 00:16:49.400
That's a shame.

00:16:49.400 --> 00:16:52.530
All right, who's the jerk
that called the cops?!

00:16:53.820 --> 00:16:55.490
Bring in the Ingrams.

00:16:55.490 --> 00:16:57.780
Put an end to this
before it gets out of hand.

00:16:57.780 --> 00:16:58.530
Roger.

00:17:02.660 --> 00:17:04.620
Get in there.
You're on your own.

00:17:04.620 --> 00:17:05.710
I'm on it.

00:17:07.920 --> 00:17:09.090
That guy!

00:17:09.090 --> 00:17:10.300
Noa, move it!

00:17:10.590 --> 00:17:12.380
Back off!
This wasn't my fault!

00:17:15.970 --> 00:17:17.470
You stupid jerk!

00:17:35.700 --> 00:17:37.200
I did it, Dad!

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:38.820
They won't get out of this one easily!

00:17:39.240 --> 00:17:40.330
You sure?

00:17:40.330 --> 00:17:43.240
You finally fixed Division 2?

00:17:43.240 --> 00:17:44.790
Yup, I really did it, Dad!

00:17:48.710 --> 00:17:51.380
What is the meaning of this?

00:17:51.380 --> 00:17:52.130
Well, Goto?!

00:17:53.630 --> 00:17:55.420
How could you let this happen?

00:17:56.050 --> 00:18:01.470
Every month I dread reading
Division 2's efficiency ratings!

00:18:01.890 --> 00:18:03.390
And then there was
yesterday's disgrace!

00:18:03.930 --> 00:18:12.020
The citizens are protesting, and
we're a complete laughingstock!

00:18:12.020 --> 00:18:17.900
Division 2 and its captain
will take full responsibility!

00:18:18.400 --> 00:18:22.240
Goto, we cannot endure this
humiliation.

00:18:22.870 --> 00:18:24.950
You and Division 2...

00:18:25.540 --> 00:18:29.040
I am also tired of this
humiliation.

00:18:29.370 --> 00:18:33.550
I have discovered that this and several
other incidents are all connected.

00:18:34.880 --> 00:18:35.380
How so?

00:18:36.210 --> 00:18:38.170
I'd like you to see something.

00:18:42.220 --> 00:18:46.560
Handwriting from the Commander
of Special Vehicles, Zen Sofue.

00:18:46.930 --> 00:18:49.560
Our forensics department
is quite astonishing.

00:18:50.270 --> 00:18:54.770
With these two samples, they
proved the same man wrote both.

00:18:56.820 --> 00:18:58.070
That's absurd!

00:18:58.650 --> 00:19:01.410
After Sofue's dismissal,
I mean, resignation...

00:19:01.410 --> 00:19:04.490
I hear that he and his son started up
a successful repair shop.

00:19:05.330 --> 00:19:09.290
Here's a picture of Zen Sofue's son.

00:19:10.790 --> 00:19:12.380
It's the same guy!

00:19:13.000 --> 00:19:16.750
And this is yesterday's
mystery man.

00:19:17.090 --> 00:19:20.880
This image was pulled from the
monitor of Officer Izumi's Ingram.

00:19:21.760 --> 00:19:24.010
What are you driving at?

00:19:24.600 --> 00:19:28.350
I want no disciplinary
action for Division 2.

00:19:28.600 --> 00:19:32.230
As for Sofue, we will
keep it our little secret.

00:19:32.900 --> 00:19:36.900
He's quite good at discovering
the skeletons in people's closets.

00:19:42.360 --> 00:19:43.410
Damn them!

00:19:43.410 --> 00:19:46.370
They're trying to pin
responsibility on me again!

00:19:54.790 --> 00:19:56.710
Get out of here, Goto!

00:19:58.760 --> 00:20:00.670
Did you hear me, Goto?!

00:20:01.300 --> 00:20:02.380
Let's do it, Dad!

00:20:10.810 --> 00:20:11.770
What's THAT?

00:20:16.770 --> 00:20:17.690
A homemade Labor?

00:20:28.870 --> 00:20:31.450
It's Judgment Day, Goto!

00:20:31.450 --> 00:20:37.090
Time to face my magnificent Labor!
Surrender while you can, Goto!

00:20:42.300 --> 00:20:44.010
Captain Goto, you're in danger!

00:20:45.300 --> 00:20:46.140
You're here!

00:20:46.140 --> 00:20:47.800
The time has finally come!

00:20:47.800 --> 00:20:50.970
You'll pay for what you did to me!

00:20:58.270 --> 00:20:59.150
Captain Goto!

00:20:59.480 --> 00:21:00.280
Goto!

00:21:02.820 --> 00:21:03.950
Fry!

00:21:14.330 --> 00:21:15.830
Everyone's against me!

00:21:15.830 --> 00:21:17.460
Stay right where you are!

00:21:18.040 --> 00:21:19.290
You'll pay!

00:21:19.500 --> 00:21:23.050
You'll pay!
You'll pay! You'll pay!

00:21:36.940 --> 00:21:38.060
Dad!

00:21:47.410 --> 00:21:49.870
Damn you, Goto!

00:21:50.160 --> 00:21:51.700
You did it to me again!

00:21:52.290 --> 00:21:56.620
You, you, you...

00:22:01.250 --> 00:22:04.670
He says he no longer blames me,
so I hope this is over.

00:22:05.260 --> 00:22:06.550
I feel sorry for him.

00:22:07.880 --> 00:22:11.050
It sure took a lot of guts
to face him down like that.

00:22:12.390 --> 00:22:18.190
Sakaki had told me before, that their
Labor was completely harmless.

00:22:19.480 --> 00:22:20.980
And that's why you acted so brave?

00:22:21.480 --> 00:22:22.690
You could say that.

00:22:23.320 --> 00:22:24.690
I give up.

00:22:25.820 --> 00:22:29.360
What are your adoring fans
going to say?

00:22:30.240 --> 00:22:31.370
I wonder.

00:22:32.530 --> 00:22:33.870
That cheater!

00:22:42.380 --> 00:22:45.590
dakishimete MIDNIGHT BLUE
Just hold me tightly, Midnight Blue

00:22:45.710 --> 00:22:49.300
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:22:51.640 --> 00:22:55.560
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:23:02.980 --> 00:23:05.070
yume ni hikizurare
Pulled into my dream I find that I wake up

00:23:05.190 --> 00:23:07.990
ore wa ase mamire no Lonely
Drenched in sweat and feeling lonely

00:23:08.070 --> 00:23:12.570
hanashi-aite no TV suitchi hipparu
I turn off the TV I've been listening to

00:23:15.240 --> 00:23:17.250
ashita ichinichi wa
Tomorrow I will spend the whole day

00:23:17.330 --> 00:23:20.080
akogareta machi no gomi no naka
In the city of my dreams, amidst the old dust

00:23:20.330 --> 00:23:24.250
hayaku mein sutoriito ni sawaritai no sa
I want to feel the main street beneath my feet soon

00:23:27.420 --> 00:23:30.760
manazashi dake wa itsu demo
I plan to always look on the brighter side

00:23:33.390 --> 00:23:36.010
ue wo muite 'ru tsumori
Keep my chin up, look to the future

00:23:35.970 --> 00:23:38.560
tatta hitotsu no michi da kara
After all, there's only one path I can travel

00:23:38.560 --> 00:23:41.770
dakishimete MIDNIGHT BLUE
Just hold me tightly, Midnight Blue

00:23:42.020 --> 00:23:45.860
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:23:48.230 --> 00:23:52.030
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:23:54.200 --> 00:23:58.080
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:24:00.410 --> 00:24:04.710
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:24:06.210 --> 00:24:09.710
This story is fiction...

00:24:06.210 --> 00:24:09.710
but in 10 years, who knows?

00:24:13.510 --> 00:24:16.350
Anybody would want to meet
pop sensation Kana Matsumoto.

00:24:16.350 --> 00:24:18.430
And that's exactly who's just
joined our Patlabor team!

00:24:18.510 --> 00:24:20.390
In honor of
National Safety Week...

00:24:20.430 --> 00:24:22.310
Kana will be controlling one of
our precious Ingrams!

00:24:22.600 --> 00:24:25.520
For some reason,
Kana may have taken a liking to me.

00:24:25.560 --> 00:24:30.150
If you don't stop monopolizing
all her time, you're gonna get it.

00:24:30.230 --> 00:24:32.110
You're not kidding are you?

00:24:32.320 --> 00:24:34.360
Next episode:
"I Love You, Miss Noa!"

00:24:34.740 --> 00:24:36.240
Target locked on!

00:24:35.870 --> 00:24:40.750
Next episode

00:24:35.870 --> 00:24:40.750
I Love You, Miss Noa
